      ":question/problem": "Consider the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dt} + y = y^{2} - 2.\n$$\n\nWhich of the following are equilibrium solutions? Select all that apply.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "An equilibrium is a constant function $y(t)=c$. Set $dy/dt=0$ and test the resulting equation.\n\nRearranging once, we need\n\n$$\nf(c)=c^{2} - c - 2=0.\n$$\n\n- For $c=1$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(1) &=\\left(1\\right)^{2} - \\left(1\\right) - 2 \\\\ &=-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis is nonzero, so it is not an equilibrium solution.\n\n- For $c=4$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(4) &=\\left(4\\right)^{2} - \\left(4\\right) - 2 \\\\ &=10\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis is nonzero, so it is not an equilibrium solution.\n\n- For $c=2$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(2) &=\\left(2\\right)^{2} - \\left(2\\right) - 2 \\\\ &=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis is zero, so it is an equilibrium solution.\n\nSelect $y=2$.",
